{
  "title": "Sorting and counting",
  "summary": "Order rows, find the top N, and count categories.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "sort_values",
      "body": [
        "```python",
        "df.sort_values(\"price\")                          # ascending",
        "df.sort_values(\"price\", ascending=False)         # descending",
        "df.sort_values([\"region\", \"price\"],",
        "               ascending=[True, False])          # region A-Z, then dearest first",
        "df.nlargest(3, \"revenue\")                        # top 3 rows by revenue",
        "df.nsmallest(2, \"price\")",
        "df.sort_index()                                  # back into index order",
        "```",
        "",
        "Sorting returns a new frame and keeps each row's index label, which is how you can still tell",
        "where a row came from. Add `.reset_index(drop=True)` when you want fresh `0, 1, 2` labels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\"Ann\", \"Bob\", \"Cy\", \"Di\"],",
        "                   \"team\": [\"B\", \"A\", \"B\", \"A\"],",
        "                   \"pts\": [7, 9, 9, 4]})",
        "print(df.sort_values(\"pts\", ascending=False)[\"name\"].tolist())",
        "print(df.sort_values([\"team\", \"pts\"])[\"name\"].tolist())",
        "print(df.nlargest(1, \"pts\").index.tolist())"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "['Bob', 'Cy', 'Ann', 'Di']",
        "['Di', 'Bob', 'Ann', 'Cy']",
        "[1]"
      ],
      "explain": "Ties keep their original order (Bob before Cy). `nlargest(1)` keeps the first of a tie unless told otherwise."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Counting categories",
      "body": [
        "```python",
        "df[\"region\"].value_counts()                 # count per value, most common first",
        "df[\"region\"].value_counts(normalize=True)   # shares that sum to 1",
        "df[\"region\"].nunique()                      # how many distinct values",
        "df[\"region\"].unique()                       # the distinct values themselves",
        "```",
        "",
        "`value_counts` returns a Series indexed by the values, named `count` (or `proportion`).",
        "It is usually the first thing you run on a text column: it reveals typos like `\"north\"`",
        "next to `\"North\"` instantly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "`df[\"region\"]` is `[\"N\", \"S\", \"N\", \"E\", \"N\"]`. What is `df[\"region\"].value_counts(normalize=True)[\"N\"]`?",
      "options": [
        "`0.6`",
        "`3`",
        "`0.333`",
        "`60`"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "3 of 5 values are N: a share of 0.6."
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Arrange the lines to print the top 2 products by revenue.",
      "lines": [
        "import io",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(\"product,qty,price\\nA,2,5.0\\nB,1,30.0\\nC,10,2.0\\n\"))",
        "df[\"revenue\"] = df[\"qty\"] * df[\"price\"]",
        "top = df.sort_values(\"revenue\", ascending=False)",
        "print(top.head(2)[\"product\"].tolist())"
      ],
      "also": [
        [
          "import pandas as pd",
          "import io",
          "df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(\"product,qty,price\\nA,2,5.0\\nB,1,30.0\\nC,10,2.0\\n\"))",
          "df[\"revenue\"] = df[\"qty\"] * df[\"price\"]",
          "top = df.sort_values(\"revenue\", ascending=False)",
          "print(top.head(2)[\"product\"].tolist())"
        ]
      ],
      "explain": "Load, derive, sort, then take the head. Prints `['B', 'C']`."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Top N",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `top_n(df, col, n)` that returns a plain list of the `name` values of the `n` rows",
        "with the largest `col`, largest first. Ties keep their original order.",
        "",
        "```python",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\"Ann\", \"Bob\", \"Cy\", \"Di\"],",
        "                   \"pts\": [7, 9, 9, 4],",
        "                   \"age\": [30, 22, 41, 35]})",
        "top_n(df, \"pts\", 2)   # [\"Bob\", \"Cy\"]",
        "top_n(df, \"age\", 3)   # [\"Cy\", \"Di\", \"Ann\"]",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef top_n(df, col, n):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def top_n(df, col, n):",
        "    return df.nlargest(n, col)[\"name\"].tolist()"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`df.nlargest(n, col)` or `sort_values(col, ascending=False, kind=\"stable\").head(n)`.",
        "Then `[\"name\"].tolist()`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\"Ann\", \"Bob\", \"Cy\", \"Di\"], \"pts\": [7, 9, 9, 4], \"age\": [30, 22, 41, 35]})",
        "Dojo.eq(\"top 2 by pts\", [\"Bob\", \"Cy\"], list(top_n(_df, \"pts\", 2)))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"top 3 by age\", [\"Cy\", \"Di\", \"Ann\"], list(top_n(_df, \"age\", 3)))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"n larger than the table\", [\"Bob\", \"Cy\", \"Ann\", \"Di\"], list(top_n(_df, \"pts\", 10)))"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bfor\\b",
          "message": "No loop"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Category shares",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `shares(df, col)` that returns a plain dict mapping each value of column `col` to its",
        "share of the rows as a **percentage** rounded to 1 decimal. The tests use this `df`:",
        "",
        "| order_id | product | region | qty | price |",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|",
        "| 1001 | Widget | North | 3 | 2.50 |",
        "| 1002 | Gadget | South | 1 | 10.00 |",
        "| 1003 | Widget | South | 5 | 2.50 |",
        "| 1004 | Gizmo | East | 2 | 7.25 |",
        "| 1005 | Gadget | North | 4 | 10.00 |",
        "| 1006 | Gizmo | North | 1 | 7.25 |",
        "",
        "```python",
        "shares(df, \"region\")   # {\"North\": 50.0, \"South\": 33.3, \"East\": 16.7}",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef shares(df, col):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def shares(df, col):",
        "    return (df[col].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100).round(1).to_dict()"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`df[col].value_counts(normalize=True)` gives fractions.",
        "`* 100`, `.round(1)`, `.to_dict()`"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import io",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.read_csv(io.StringIO('order_id,product,region,qty,price\\n1001,Widget,North,3,2.50\\n1002,Gadget,South,1,10.00\\n1003,Widget,South,5,2.50\\n1004,Gizmo,East,2,7.25\\n1005,Gadget,North,4,10.00\\n1006,Gizmo,North,1,7.25\\n'))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"regions\", {\"North\": 50.0, \"South\": 33.3, \"East\": 16.7}, shares(_df, \"region\"))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"products\", {\"Widget\": 33.3, \"Gadget\": 33.3, \"Gizmo\": 33.3}, shares(_df, \"product\"))"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "value_counts",
          "message": "Uses value_counts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Sort by team A-Z, then points highest first.",
      "code": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\"team\": [\"B\", \"A\", \"A\"], \"pts\": [5, 2, 8]})",
        "out = df.sort_values(__1__, ascending=__2__)",
        "print(out[\"pts\"].tolist())"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        [
          "[\"team\", \"pts\"]"
        ],
        [
          "[True, False]"
        ]
      ],
      "bank": [
        "[\"pts\", \"team\"]",
        "[False, True]",
        "False"
      ],
      "explain": "Prints `[8, 2, 5]`: team A first (8 before 2), then team B."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Leaderboard",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `leaderboard(df)` for a table with `name` and `score` columns. Return a new DataFrame:",
        "",
        "- sorted by `score` highest first, and by `name` A-Z when scores tie,",
        "- with a fresh index `0, 1, 2, ...`,",
        "- with a `rank` column `1, 2, 3, ...` as the **first** column (then `name`, `score`).",
        "",
        "```python",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\"Cid\", \"Bea\", \"Al\"], \"score\": [75, 90, 75]})",
        "leaderboard(df)",
        "#    rank name  score",
        "# 0     1  Bea     90",
        "# 1     2  Al      75",
        "# 2     3  Cid     75",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef leaderboard(df):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def leaderboard(df):",
        "    out = df.sort_values([\"score\", \"name\"], ascending=[False, True]).reset_index(drop=True)",
        "    out.insert(0, \"rank\", range(1, len(out) + 1))",
        "    return out"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`sort_values([\"score\", \"name\"], ascending=[False, True])` then `.reset_index(drop=True)`.",
        "`out.insert(0, \"rank\", range(1, len(out) + 1))` puts a column first."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "import pandas as _pd",
        "_df = _pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\"Cid\", \"Bea\", \"Al\"], \"score\": [75, 90, 75]})",
        "_out = leaderboard(_df)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"columns\", [\"rank\", \"name\", \"score\"], list(_out.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"names in order\", [\"Bea\", \"Al\", \"Cid\"], _out[\"name\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"ranks\", [1, 2, 3], [int(v) for v in _out[\"rank\"].tolist()])",
        "Dojo.eq(\"fresh index\", [0, 1, 2], _out.index.tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"the input is unchanged\", [\"Cid\", \"Bea\", \"Al\"], _df[\"name\"].tolist())"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
